    "skills": [],
    "fullText": "CLSA Securities Korea Ltd. is seeking a qualified and experienced candidate for the position of Settlement Officer within its Korea Operations team.\n\nJob description\nAn opportunity exists for an experienced professional to join our Operations team in Korea as a Settlement Officer. The successful candidate will be responsible for trade support and settlement activities across cash equities, futures and options, overseas bond products, and outbound trading services for domestic clients in Korea. The role will also support the enhancement of existing internal controls and operational requirements.\n\nOpening position: Settlement Officer, Operations\nStart date: Immediate availability preferred\nEmployment Type: Permanent Position/Full-Time\nLocation: 30th Floor, One IFC, 10 Gukjegeumyung-ro, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul, 07326, Korea\nNumber of Openings : 2\nWorking Hours: 8 hours per day (excluding 1 hour for lunchtime)\nCompensation: A competitive remuneration package will be offered to the successful candidate, based on experience and qualifications.\nApplication Deadline: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.\nHow to Apply: Candidates whose qualifications and experience align with the requirements of the role are invited to submit their CV in English to hr.korea@clsa.com . Or directly apply to https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466187391/.\nApplications will be treated with strict confidence.\n\nPosition Description\n? As part of the trade support / settlement team, we are responsible for processing cash equities and F&O settlements.\n? Engaged in overseas bond settlements for Treasury Liquidity Investment and ETF/ Single Stock Market Making Business.\n? Supporting outbound trades for Korea domestic clients.\n? Improving existing internal control and requirements.\n\nKey Areas of Responsibilities\n? Perform daily middle and back office operations and respond on internal and external client’s inquires.\n? Liaising with overseas operations to complete cash equities trades matching on daily trading support and administrations issues.\n? Monitor daily trade cycle and resolve the breaks, perform daily trades reconciliation.\n? Processing Korea Clients On-Boarding and accounts setup and static management.\n? Release outbound confirmations for KR domestic clients and monitoring settlement status.\n? Back up the overall operation/settlement in both cash equities, F&O, and other business.\n? Preparation of Regulatory reporting to FSS, KRX, KSFC, BOK and etc.\n? Participate in projects as assigned.\n\nRequirement\n? Degree holder, preferred major in Business, Finance or Accounting related discipline\n? Minimum 5 years of experience in Operations/Middle Office within Securities Brokerage Industries\n? Familiarity with cross-border investment via QFI, Stock Connect and Bond Connect\n? Knowledge of investment products such as equities, fixed income, future, option, FX and etc.\n? Strong sense of accountability and responsibilities for owning issues through to resolution.\n? Strong Communicator (articulate and literate), highly self-motivated, attentive to details, diligent and a good team player.\n? Proficiency in both spoken and written English and Korean.\n\nIf you are interested in this opportunity and believe your qualifications align with the requirements outlined above, please submit your resume in English to mari.jang@clsa.com.\n\nAbout CLSA\nCLSA established a presence in Korea in 1996, and moved from being a branch to a subsidiary in 2003. CITIC CLSA Korea is licensed with Financial Services Commission(FSC) and Financial Supervisory Service (FSS) as \"Brokerage & Dealing including Underwriting and ETF Business\". This permits full scope of brokerage business for investors into the Korea market. The office has a dedicated team of 66 and operates a brokerage for securities, ETF and exchange-traded futures and options as well as debt capital markets business.",
