    "fullText": "CLSA Securities Korea Ltd. is seeking a qualified and experienced candidate for the position of Sales Assistant within Equity Sales team for Korea.\n\nOpening position: Sales Assistant, Institutional Equities\n\nStart date: Immediate availability preferred\nEmployment Type: Permanent Position/Full-Time\nLocation: 30th Floor, One IFC, 10 Gukjegeumyung-ro, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul, 07326, Korea\nNumber of Openings : 1\nWorking Hours: 8 hours per day (excluding 1 hour for lunchtime)\nCompensation: A competitive remuneration package will be offered to the successful candidate, based on experience and qualifications.\nApplication Deadline: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.\nHow to Apply: Candidates whose qualifications and experience align with the requirements of the role are invited to submit the CV in English to yuna.lee@clsa.com.\nApplications will be treated with strict confidence.\n\nPosition Description\n? CLSA Korea is seeking a Sales Assistant to provide support to the Equity Sales team in various areas such as fostering business relationships, maximizing revenue, promoting and marketing CLSA products, and ensuring daily client service.\n\nKey Areas of Responsibilities\n? Assist sales team members to coordinate and execute new marketing initiatives, client seminars, brand building events and promotional campaigns\n? Assist sales team members to develop new products, services, sales and distribution channels\n? Translate local news flow from Korean to English on a daily basis\n? Assist with inbound client’s company visits in Korea and translation if required\n? Other Sales team duties as assigned\n\nRequirement\n? Bachelor degree holder in Finance or relevant discipline(s)\n? Good understanding of Bloomberg, Quantiwise, Check Terminal and other financial information providers preferred but not a must\n? Possesses high standards for excellence and takes ownership of the work\n? Self-motivated, diligent?, capable of multi-tasking with a strong emphasis on attention to detail.\n? Highly proficient in Excel and possesses good numeracy skills\n? Well rounded, and a team player\n? Fluent in both written and verbal English, with knowledge of Chinese language as an added advantage\n\nAbout CLSA\nCLSA established a presence in Korea in 1996, and moved from being a branch to a subsidiary in 2003. CITIC CLSA Korea is licensed with Financial Services Commission(FSC) and Financial Supervisory Service (FSS) as \"Brokerage & Dealing including Underwriting and ETF Business\". This permits full scope of brokerage business for investors into the Korea market. The office has a dedicated team of 66 and operates a brokerage for securities, ETF and exchange-traded futures and options as well as debt capital markets business.",
