    "fullText": "Tcha Partners Asset Management - Analyst Position\n\nTcha Partners is a fast-growing Seoul-based asset manager with approximately KRW306bn in AUM. The team consists of experienced professionals from Macquarie and global energy companies.\n\nThe Infrastructure Investment Division manages a portfolio that includes quasi-public bus operators and energy stations, with a strong focus on identifying and pursuing investment opportunities in the mobility and clean energy sectors. We are actively seeking to expand our team with a highly motivated individual to support the daily operations of our private equity funds.\n\n1. Position: Analyst (Infrastructure Investment Division)\n\n2. Starting date: ASAP preferred\n\n3. Qualifications:\n- 1-3 years of relevant professional experience\n- Certified Public Accountant (KICPA / AICPA / equivalent) preferred\n- Financial modeling (Excel) and presentation (PowerPoint) skills required\n- Analytical and quantitative skills\n- Ability to work well in a fast-paced environment\n- Prior experience in Private Equity, Infrastructure investment, Project Finance, Investment Banking, or related fields is highly preferred\n- Bilingual (Korean and English) highly preferred\n\n4. Responsibilities:\n- Support the execution of M&A and investment transactions, including initial screening, industry and market research, and preparation of internal investment memoranda and investment committee materials.\n- Build and maintain financial models, including LBO and Greenfield/Brownfield investment models, and perform valuation and return analysis to support investment decisions\n- Support due diligence and transaction execution, coordinating with external advisors (accounting, legal, tax, and technical) and consolidating their findings into internal reports.\n- Assist in the review and preparation of key transaction documents, including share purchase agreements (SPA), loan agreements, and shareholders’ agreements (SHA).\n- Monitor portfolio company performance, including periodic financial and operational analysis, KPI and covenant tracking, and support for value creation initiatives.\n- Support fund operations and investor relations, including quarterly reporting, capital calls and distributions, and responses to LP inquiries.\n\n5. Application: Send your English resume with the subject line [Analyst Application_First Name Last Name] along with Consent to Collect and Use Personal Data (separately attached) to \"hr@tchapartners.com\"\n\n6. Deadline: Oct 9, 2026. However, early submission is highly recommended as interviews will be conducted on a rolling basis",
