    "isDemo": false,
    "skills": [],
    "fullText": "CGS International Securities Hong Kong Limited, Korea Branch\n(씨지에스 인터내셔널증권 홍콩 한국지점) 15F S-Tower, 82 Saemunan-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul 03185, Korea\n\nJob description\n\nAn opportunity exists for a dule-role professional to join our team in Korea as a Junior Institutional Equity Domestic Sales & CFD RM (Relationship Management). This role combines driving domestic institutional equity sales with managing regional CFD business relationships, client serving, and stakeholder coordination.\n\nJob opening position: Junior Institutional Equity Domestic Sales & CFD RM\n\n? Start date: ASAP (exact date TBD)\n? Employment Type: Permanent Position\n? Positions open: 1\n? Working Hours: 8 hours per day (excluding 1 hour for lunchtime) / Up to 52 hours per week\n? Salary: It is in accordance with the Company’s rule.\n? Deadline for CV Submission: Until the recruitment closing\n\nKey Responsibilities (About the Role)\n\n? Institutional Equity Domestic Sales\n? Build and maintain strong relationships with domestic institutional PMs and Buyside Analysts.\n? Deliver CGSI research insights and promote actionable trading ideas to generate equity revenue.\n? Coordinate corporate access, including NDRs and analysts’ briefings for domestic clients.\n\n? CFD Relationship Management\n? Act as the primary point of contact between Korean securities firms and the regional CFD business team.\n? Build and maintain strong relationships with institutional clients and key stakeholders.\n? Facilitate effective communication between Korea Brokers, Compliance, and Risk teams.\n\nWhat You’ll Need\n? Entry-level\n? Preferred minimum 1 --2 Years of relevant experience in the financial industry especially, as a Research Assistant (RA) or Research intern\n? Bachelor’s Degree\n? fluency in English and Korean\n? Strong verbal and written Communication Skills\n? Proficiency in Microsoft Office\n\nCandidates who are interested and meet the requirements delineated above should send their detailed Resumes & Cover Letters in English by e-mail to minjoo.lee@cgsi.com.\n______________________________________________________________\n\nAbout China Galaxy International (CGI) Financial Holdings Limited\n\nChina Galaxy International Financial Holdings Limited (China Galaxy International) was incorporated in Hong Kong on 9th February 2011 and is a wholly owned subsidiary of China Galaxy Securities Co. Ltd. (China Galaxy Securities).\n\nChina Galaxy Securities (CGS) is one of the leading integrated service providers in the PRC for the securities industry. The Group provides comprehensive securities services including brokerage, sales and trading, investment banking and investment management.\n\nChina Galaxy Securities has the largest securities distribution network in n PRC with 5 subsidiaries, 37 branches and over 501 securities branches covering 31 provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities across China. It also services one of the largest client bases in the PRC of over 13.22 million brokerage clients (as of 31st December 2021) . China Galaxy Securities is a joint stock limited company listed on both Hong Kong Stock Exchange and Shanghai Stock Exchange.\n\nCGS International Securities Hong Kong Ltd, Korea branch (CGS Korea) became the first ASEAN financial institution to obtain an equities brokerage license in South Korea since 2002, enabling us to serve both our domestic and international clients.\n\nCGS Korea is now in the position to offer its global clients access to the South Korean equity market and to catalyze business and investment flows between South Korea and Asia. CGS Korea also provides corporate advisory services and research coverage to both domestic and international clients. Consistently ranked among the top in Asia (ex. Japan), our regional research team oversees economic, industry, market, and stock-specific data to enhance the performance of clients’ global portfolio.",
